No that's intentional as I mentioned in the comment:
```
// We don't bypass the whole logic to check templates because third-parties might have
// Mono-enabled UWP builds using this path.
```

The idea is that if you do provide templates which you got from a third-party and which would work, then you can use them. But if you don't, then it will just inform that the official Godot Mono doesn't support UWP.
